OL,3,GNEWSAI couldn't reach Wales' highest
OL,4,Asummit because people jumped the queue
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Helen Pacey and her family booked
OL,7,Fa trip on the Snowdon Mountain Railway,
OL,8,Fthey were looking forward to touching
OL,9,Fthe summit marker at the top of Yr
OL,10,FWyddfa, also known as Snowdon.
OL,12,FBut after spending 30 minutes waiting
OL,13,Fin a queue at the top of Wales' highest
OL,14,Fmountain, 58-year-old Helen ran out of
OL,15,Ftime and had to get the return train
OL,16,Fback down.
OL,18,F"I've had both my hips replaced, so
OL,19,Fthere was no way I could have gone up
OL,20,Fthe rocky side of it," said Helen, from
OL,21,FHull in Yorkshire.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
